[{:db/id -1, :adr/id "adr-2605261215-hodoki-elv-disassembly-tier-b-actor-r0", :adr/title "ADR-2605261215: hodoki (解き) — End-of-Life Vehicle Disassembly + Materials Recovery Tier-B Actor R0 Scaffold", :adr/status "proposed", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/body "\n# ADR-2605261215: hodoki (解き) — End-of-Life Vehicle Disassembly + Materials Recovery Tier-B Actor R0 Scaffold\n\n**Status**: proposed\n**Date**: 2026-05-26\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki (author), Council Lv6+ (ratify)\n**ADR Hierarchy**: Sibling of ADR-2605242000 (wadachi mobility), ADR-2605252400 (kanayama metallurgy), ADR-2605261115 (makura foam pillows). Upstream feeder for kanayama (metals) + makura (seat foam circular) + silicon Wave 2 (electronics). Parent constitutional: ADR-2605192200 §2(c) (anti-surveillance applied to vehicles) + §2(h) (circular economy) + §2(e) (anti-gatekeeping via right-to-repair).\n\n## Context\n\nEnd-of-life vehicle (ELV) recycling is dominated globally by oligopoly auto-recyclers operating opaque shredding facilities. Material recovery rates plateau at ~85% (EU ELV Directive 2000/53/EC mandates 95% by mass since 2015, but compliance is partial and PGM/Li-ion handling is frequently outsourced). Several constitutional gaps remain unaddressed by the commodity ELV industry:\n\n1. **Surveillance data exfiltration risk**: Modern vehicles (especially premium Audi / BMW / Tesla / VW-group) carry ECU + infotainment + telematics data — GPS history, contacts, paired phones, drive recordings, voice samples — that survive scrapping and is routinely extracted by data brokers. ADR-2605192200 §2(c) (anti-surveillance) applies directly: religious-corp adherents cannot trust commodity recyclers with vehicle data.\n2. **Right-to-repair gatekeeping**: OEMs monetize parts scarcity via opaque used-parts markets + anti-disassembly DRM. ADR-2605192200 §2(e) (anti-gatekeeping) calls for first-party parts cataloging with full VIN provenance.\n3. **F-gas atmospheric venting**: MAC (mobile air conditioning) refrigerant (R1234yf / R134a) is frequently vented during shredding despite §2(g) environmental harm prohibition.\n4. **Li-ion second-life misclassification**: BEV/PHEV batteries with >70% SoH are routinely shredded for material recovery when they could serve stationary storage (hikari R2+ consumer); §2(h) circular economy violation.\n5. **PGM (Pt/Pd/Rh) leakage to ASR**: Catalytic converter PGMs are frequently undercaptured (~70-85% industry baseline vs ≥95% feasible).\n6. **No cross-actor circular feed**: Seat foam, textile, glass, ferrous, non-ferrous, electronics could feed kanayama / makura / silicon as upstream feedstock, but commodity recyclers have no such routing.\n\nThe user-prompted source reference for this design is the manufacturing methodology survey in the YouTube video \"How Audi Strips Down Thousand of Like-New Expensive Cars Inside Massive Facility\" (whyjio70IUU, 2026), depicting a large-scale OEM-run ELV disassembly + parts-harvest facility. The mechanical methodology (depollution → harvest → shred → sort) is adopted; the OEM-monopoly right-to-repair-restricting layer is rejected per §2(e).\n\nUntil this ADR, religious-corp has no Tier-B actor covering ELV disassembly. `wadachi` is autonomous-mobility R&D (vehicle build-side, R0); `kanayama` is circular metallurgy (downstream consumer of shred output); `makura` is foam pillow manufacturing (downstream consumer of seat foam, G13 take-back invariant). Without `hodoki`:\n\n1. Adherent-owned vehicles at end-of-life have no constitutionally-compliant recycling path (data wipe + ≥95% material recovery + right-to-repair parts catalog).\n2. `kanayama` and `makura` G13 circular-material invariants depend on guaranteed upstream feedstock — without `hodoki` the loop has no first-party origin.\n3. `silicon` Wave 2 cannot close its loop (vehicle ECU PCBs are a major rare-metal source: Ag/Au/Pd/Cu).\n\nThis ADR fulfills that gap, declaring 14 constitutional gates and 10 non-goals, and lands a 9-cell Pregel scaffold whose `solve()` methods raise `RuntimeError` until R1 activation.\n\n## Decision\n\n### 1. Actor identity\n\n| Field | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Actor name | `hodoki` |\n| Japanese | 解き (continuative noun of 解く to untie / dissolve / unmake; Buddhist 解脱 release echo — vehicles released from compound form back to elemental materials, then reborn through kanayama / makura / silicon) |\n| Display name | `解き (hodoki)` |\n| Tier (ADR-2605192415 §B) | **B** — per-domain leader, sibling of `kanayama` / `wadachi` / `makura` / `kuni-umi` / `yakushi` / `watatsumi` / `tatekata` |\n| Path-based DID | `did:web:etzhayyim.com:hodoki` |\n| Per-vehicle DID pattern (reserved) | `did:web:etzhayyim.com:hodoki:vehicle:<vin>` |\n| Per-part DID pattern (reserved) | `did:web:etzhayyim.com:hodoki:part:<lotId>:<partSerial>` |\n| Repo location | `20-actors/hodoki/` |\n| Lexicon namespace | `com.etzhayyim.hodoki.*` |\n| License | Apache 2.0 + Charter Compliance Rider v2.0 |\n\n### 2. Scope (R0)\n\n**In scope (R0–R1):**\n\n- M1 passenger vehicles (≤2.5t curb weight, ≤8 seats including driver per EU 2007/46/EC)\n- Powertrains: gasoline ICE / diesel ICE / HEV / PHEV / BEV (battery class restricted to NMC / LFP / NCA; cell-recovery via Wave 2 ADR)\n- Full disassembly chain: intake audit → depollution → battery handling → parts harvest → catalyst recovery → seat/textile recovery → shred → material sort → cross-actor feed (kanayama metals + makura foam/textile + silicon electronics)\n\n**Explicitly deferred to R2+ (separate ADR + Council Lv6+ supermajority):**\n\n- N1/N2/N3/N4 class vehicles (buses, trucks ≥3.5t, semi-trailers) — Wave 2 ADR\n- Hydrogen fuel-cell vehicles (high-pressure H2 tank disassembly requires separate Wave + safety review)\n- Tesla-class proprietary battery cell harvest without OEM cooperation — Wave 2 ADR\n- E-waste integrated PCB/IC co-processing (separate WEEE ADR; silicon Wave 2 dependency)\n\n**Constitutional non-goals (R0–R3, immutable; amendment requires Council Lv6+ supermajority + new ADR):** see §4 below.\n\n### 3. 5-Layer ELV Processing Chain\n\nAdopted from mature OEM-run ELV facility practice (depollution → parts harvest → shred → sort); religious-corp-ised by mandatory data-wipe, right-to-repair parts catalog, ≥95% material recovery, ≥95% F-gas capture, ≥95% PGM recovery, and Li-ion second-life classification.\n\n| Layer | Stage | Key technology | Religious-corp constraints |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **L1** | 受入 + 除染 (intake + depollution) | VIN title verification + prior-owner consent + telemetry-data wipe attestation (G8); fluid drain (fuel / oil / coolant / brake / windshield washer); MAC refrigerant capture (R1234yf / R134a / R290); airbag pyrotechnic neutralization; battery disconnect | G5 Charter scan per intake (no military vehicles N1); G6 F-gas ≥95% capture; G7 airbag pyrotechnic safe-disposal SOP; G8 cryptographic ECU + infotainment data wipe BEFORE any disassembly; G10 SBT-gated refrigerant + airbag + Li-ion operators |\n| **L2** | 蓄電池処理 (battery handling) | Li-ion battery state-of-health classification: SoH ≥70% → second-life routing (hikari R2+ stationary storage consumer); SoH <70% → cell-recycle routing (Wave 2 ADR feedstock); lead-acid → Pb recovery via kanayama Wave 3 | G7 thermal-safety SOP: no puncture, no short-circuit, thermal-runaway-containment cell enclosure; G11 KPI cap NMC/NCA + LFP only (no NiMH cell recovery in R0); SoH measurement IPFS-pinned (G2) |\n| **L3** | 部品取出 + 触媒回収 + シート回収 (parts harvest + catalyst recovery + seat-textile recovery) | Reusable parts identification + IPFS-pinned parts catalog with VIN provenance (G12 right-to-repair); catalytic converter brick removal + PGM smelter handoff; seat foam + textile recovery + bilingual sorting + makura G13 circular feed | G12 right-to-repair invariant — every harvested part published; no proprietary lock-in; G14 PGM recovery ≥95% (Pt/Pd/Rh); cross-actor circular feed (makura seat foam, G13 invariant closure) |\n| **L4** | 車体破砕 (body shred) | Hulk shredder + magnetic + eddy-current + density (ASR sink/float) sorting; ferrous → kanayama Wave 2 (steel R3), non-ferrous Al → kanayama Wave 1, Cu wire → kanayama Wave 3, ASR (auto shredder residue) | G13 ≥95% material recovery rate; ASR <5% mass to landfill; ASR composition disclosed (PVC / glass-fiber / paint / dust) |\n| **L5** | 排出監査 + 来歴記録 (emissions audit + provenance binder) | F-gas leakage continuous monitoring; ASR composition + ASR landfill mass; PGM yield audit; full chain DID anchoring (input VIN → output parts catalog + material lots + emissions) on kotoba-datomic | G2 mass-balance audit ≥98% closure on kotoba-datomic (input vehicle mass = parts + material lots + emissions); G14 PGM yield audit; G13 ASR mass cap |\n\n### 4. Constitutional Gates (G1–G14, IMMUTABLE R0–R3)\n\n| Gate | Requirement | Rationale |\n|---|---|---|\n| **G1** | All depollution + dismantling + shredder firmware, all CAD for fixtures + tooling, **open-source** (Apache 2.0 + Charter Rider) | §2(b) anti-secrecy |\n| **G2** | **Mass-balance audit ≥98% closure on kotoba-datomic** (input vehicle curb-weight = output parts mass + material-lot mass + emission mass + ASR mass); per-vehicle attestation | Inherits kanayama G2 cross-cell invariant pattern; novel application to ELV |\n| **G3** | Every critical step (refrigerant capture, battery disconnect, airbag neutralization, PGM brick removal) signed by **witness quorum ≥2 distinct robots** (Ed25519, DID-bound) | ADR-2605191524 swarm broadcast |\n| **G4** | All parts catalog entries + material recovery reports + take-back records **JP + EN bilingual minimum** | §2(e) anti-gatekeeping of repair information |\n| **G5** | All vehicle intakes pass **Charter Rider §2(a-h) scan** (no military / no weapon-carrying / no covertly-modified vehicles); rejected intakes route to Council Lv6+ review | §2(a) + N1 |\n| **G6** | **F-gas (HFC / HFO refrigerant) capture ≥95% by mass** per vehicle; continuous leak monitoring; no atmospheric venting under any circumstance | §2(g) environmental; UNEP Montreal Protocol Kigali Amendment alignment |\n| **G7** | **Li-ion battery thermal-safety SOP** — no puncture, no short-circuit, thermal-runaway-containment cell enclosure required during all handling; SoH measurement per battery + cell where accessible | §1.13 worker wellbecoming + §2(g) thermal-event environmental risk |\n| **G8** | **MANDATORY ECU + infotainment + telematics data wipe BEFORE any disassembly** — cryptographic destruction attestation with ≥2 robot witness signatures; if wipe fails (sealed module), the entire ECU is physically destroyed (chip-shred) with attestation | **CONSTITUTIONAL FIRST**: §2(c) anti-surveillance applied to consumer vehicles (parallel to makura G14 + N9 anti-surveillance applied to pillows) |\n| **G9** | Inference paths (parts identification, defect classification, SoH estimation, fluid type detection) use **Murakumo no-VKE mesh only** (ADR-2605214000 / ADR-2605215000) | Constitutional inference invariant |\n| **G10** | Refrigerant + airbag + Li-ion + PGM + ECU-shred operations are **SBT-gated personnel**; non-SBT visitors require 1 SBT = 1 vote Council review | §1.13 worker wellbecoming |\n| **G11** | KPI caps R0–R1: **M1 passenger class only**, ≤2.5t curb weight, ≤8 seats. **N2/N3/N4 (buses, trucks ≥3.5t)** = Wave 2 ADR required. **Hydrogen fuel-cell** = Wave 2 ADR required. **Tesla cell-recovery without OEM cooperation** = Wave 2 ADR required. Council Lv6+ to amend | Prevent scope creep + premium safety review for higher-risk classes |\n| **G12** | **RIGHT-TO-REPAIR INVARIANT**: every harvested part has IPFS-pinned catalog entry with VIN provenance + part DID + condition grade + bilingual description + open price discovery; no proprietary lock-in; no anti-disassembly DRM tolerated | **CONSTITUTIONAL FIRST**: §2(e) anti-gatekeeping of repair operationalized at vehicle scale |\n| **G13** | **≥95% material recovery rate by mass** (target ≥97% by R3, exceeds EU ELV Directive); ASR <5% mass to landfill; ASR composition disclosed; **cross-actor circular feed mandatory** to kanayama (ferrous + non-ferrous + Cu) + makura (seat foam + textile, G13 invariant closure) + silicon Wave 2 (ECU PCB rare metals) | §2(h) circular economy operationalized as cross-actor invariant |\n| **G14** | **PGM (Pt / Pd / Rh) recovery yield ≥95%** from catalytic converters; cell-level audit of PGM smelter receipts; no PGM leak to ASR fraction | §2(h) circular economy; high-value scarce-material conservation |\n\n### 5. Non-Goals (N1–N10, IMMUTABLE R0–R3)\n\nCharter Rider §2(a) + §2(c) + §2(g) + §1.13 + §1.15 + commercial / safety boundary anchors:\n\n| ID | Excluded scope | Reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| **N1** | **Military vehicles** (tanks, MRAPs, AFVs, military trucks, military trailers, military motorcycles) | §2(a) constitutional |\n| **N2** | **Aerospace vehicles** (aircraft, helicopters, drones ≥25 kg MTOW, gliders) | Separate aerospace Tier-B if/when needed |\n| **N3** | **Marine vessels** (ships, boats, yachts, jet-skis) | watatsumi-adjacent or separate ADR |\n| **N4** | **Rail rolling stock** (locomotives, freight cars, passenger coaches, light-rail vehicles) | kuni-umi rail-adjacent or separate ADR |\n| **N5** | **Buses / trucks ≥3.5t** (N2 / N3 class commercial vehicles) | Wave 2 ADR + Council Lv6+ supermajority; different battery scale + airbag pattern + hydraulic systems |\n| **N6** | **Vehicles with proprietary anti-disassembly DRM** unless OEM cooperation explicitly granted (refusing DRM circumvention preserves §2(b) constitutional posture) | §2(b) + legal-clarity invariant |\n| **N7** | **VIN-stolen / criminal-provenance vehicles** — only documented title chain accepted; Charter scan + Council escalation on suspect intakes | Title invariant + §2(a) anti-organized-crime |\n| **N8** | **Vehicle parts re-sale for re-VIN'ing (chop shop)** — every harvested part carries permanent VIN provenance + cannot be used to forge identity of a different vehicle | Title invariant; §2(a) anti-organized-crime |\n| **N9** | **Tesla-class proprietary battery cell harvest without OEM cooperation** (cell-level recovery only via Wave 2 ADR) | §2(b) + safety + legal-clarity |\n| **N10** | **Hydrogen fuel-cell vehicles** (high-pressure H2 tank disassembly requires Wave 2 ADR with dedicated thermal + pressure safety review) | Safety-class boundary; §1.13 worker wellbecoming + §2(g) explosion risk |\n\n### 6. 9 Pregel Cells + Murakumo Placement (R0 design-only)\n\n| Cell | Layer | Murakumo node | Phase |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `elv_intake_audit` | L1a | naphtali | VIN title verification + prior-owner consent + Charter §2(a-h) scan + initial data-wipe attestation request |\n| `elv_depollution` | L1b | joseph | Fluid drain (fuel / oil / coolant / brake / washer) + MAC refrigerant capture + airbag pyrotechnic neutralization + battery disconnect |\n| `elv_battery_handling` | L2 | levi | Li-ion SoH classification (≥70% second-life → hikari; <70% cell-recycle → Wave 2); lead-acid → kanayama Wave 3; thermal-safety enforcement |\n| `elv_parts_harvest` | L3a | simeon | Reusable parts identification + condition grading + IPFS-pinned catalog publication (G12 right-to-repair) |\n| `elv_catalyst_recovery` | L3b | levi | Catalytic converter brick removal + PGM smelter handoff + yield audit (G14 ≥95% Pt/Pd/Rh) |\n| `elv_seat_textile_recovery` | L3c | dan | Seat foam + textile recovery; bilingual sorting; **cross-actor feed to makura** (G13 invariant closure) |\n| `elv_body_shred` | L4 | zebulun | Hulk shredder + magnetic + eddy-current + density sort; ferrous + non-ferrous Al + Cu wire + ASR streams |\n| `elv_emissions_audit` | cross-cutting | levi | F-gas leakage continuous; ASR mass + composition; PGM yield audit; per-vehicle compliance log |\n| `elv_provenance_binder` | terminal | judah | Full chain DID anchoring on kotoba-datomic (input VIN → parts catalog + material lots + emissions + ASR mass) |\n\n### 7. Robotics Classes\n\n**New (R0 reservation only — physical builds blocked behind R1 ADR):**\n\n| Class | Role | Phase |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Hagasu (剥がす)** | Paint / body-panel stripper; thermal + mechanical detachment | R1+ |\n| **Nuku (抜く)** | Fluid-drain manipulator with sealed drain ports for fuel / oil / coolant / refrigerant (G6 ≥95% capture) | R1+ |\n| **Tokike (解け)** | Body-fastener releaser (bolt / clip / rivet unfastener with vision-guided targeting; namesake mini-robot of the actor) | R1+ |\n\n**Inherited (reuse, no specialization required in R0):**\n\n- kanayama Yokin (molten-metal pour) — R2+ for PGM bench smelter operations\n- kuni-umi Otete (general manipulation) — parts handling\n- kuni-umi Mimi (metrology) — SoH measurement + dimensional + condition grading\n- kuni-umi Quad (logistics) — vehicle intake transport + ASR drum handling\n\n### 8. Lexicon Namespace (8 record types, R0 stubs)\n\n```\ncom.etzhayyim.hodoki.{\n  elvIntakeRecord                # L1a — VIN + title + prior-owner consent + Charter scan\n  depollutionAttestation         # L1b — fluid drain + F-gas + airbag + battery disconnect\n  batteryHandlingRecord          # L2 — Li-ion SoH + routing (second-life vs cell-recycle)\n  partsHarvestCatalog            # L3a — IPFS-pinned parts catalog with VIN provenance (G12)\n  catalystRecoveryRecord         # L3b — PGM brick + smelter handoff + yield audit\n  shredOutputAttestation         # L4 — ferrous + non-ferrous + Cu + ASR mass + cross-actor handoff\n  dataWipeAttestation            # G8 — ECU + infotainment + telematics cryptographic destruction\n  silenDeconstructionReview      # Council 5-of-7 attestation, all new vehicle classes / OEM cooperation\n}\n```\n\nSchema details deferred to R1 ADR.\n\n### 9. 4-Phase Roadmap\n\n| Phase | Scope | Trigger |\n|---|---|---|\n| **R0** (this wave) | Scaffold only; 9 cells RuntimeError; 8 lexicon stubs | ADR-2605261215 |\n| **R1** | Benchtop single-vehicle hand-disassembly + data-wipe demonstration + Hagasu / Nuku / Tokike robot prototypes; 5-vehicle trial cohort | ADR-2605261230 + Council Lv6+ + certified ELV-recycler SME + certified F-gas refrigerant technician SME |\n| **R2** | Pilot ≤10 vehicles/day continuous depollution + parts harvest + shred + cross-actor feed (kanayama + makura + silicon); tatekata-shared yard allocation; right-to-repair parts catalog live | ADR-2605261245 + 30-day public comment + cross-actor circular feed stand-up |\n| **R3** | Community-scale ≤500 vehicles/month + ≥95% material recovery + ≥95% F-gas capture + ≥95% PGM yield + 60-day public review; LANDS.md amendment if dedicated yard | ADR-2605261300 + 60-day public review |\n\nReserved ADR slots: 2605261230 (R1), 2605261245 (R2), 2605261300 (R3).\n\n## Consequences\n\n**Positive:**\n\n- Adherents gain first-party constitutionally-compliant ELV recycling path with mandatory data-wipe (G8) + right-to-repair parts catalog (G12) + ≥95% material recovery (G13)\n- `kanayama` G2 mass-balance + circular invariant gains its first dedicated upstream feedstock origin (ferrous + Al + Cu)\n- `makura` G13 take-back invariant gains cross-actor circular feed (seat foam → pillow crumb blend)\n- `silicon` Wave 2 gains automotive ECU PCB feedstock (Ag / Au / Pd / Cu) once Wave 2 ADR ratifies\n- Establishes the **§2(c) anti-surveillance applied to vehicles** pattern (G8) — parallel to makura G14 (consumer goods)\n- Establishes the **right-to-repair operationalization** pattern (G12) — parts catalog as constitutional public-interest disclosure\n- Establishes the **cross-actor circular feed** as a multilateral constitutional invariant (G13 binds hodoki ↔ kanayama ↔ makura ↔ silicon)\n\n**Negative / risks:**\n\n- ECU cryptographic data-wipe (G8) is technically difficult for sealed modules with no documented wipe API; fallback to physical chip-shred raises material-recovery cost\n- F-gas capture ≥95% (G6) requires specialized closed-loop refrigerant recovery equipment (~$30K per station) — R2 CAPEX risk\n- Right-to-repair parts catalog (G12) may invite OEM legal pressure (right-to-repair litigation in JP / EU / US still evolving) — Council legal advisory required\n- N6 anti-DRM-circumvention posture means certain vehicle classes (modern Tesla / VW MQB / BMW ix) may be functionally non-disassemblable without OEM cooperation — R0 scope reduction\n- Li-ion second-life classification (L2) requires certified battery test bench; SoH measurement standard varies by OEM — R1 SME critical-path\n- ASR <5% to landfill (G13) is aggressive vs EU baseline 10-15%; may require thermal-recovery partner (kanayama or external) — R3 risk\n\n**Mitigation:**\n\n- G8 wipe API research is Council-funded SME effort in R1 prep; physical chip-shred fallback is acceptable per ADR §G8\n- F-gas station CAPEX shared with tatekata yard; recovered refrigerant sold to Council-approved reclaimers as donation-receipt\n- G12 right-to-repair legal review by Council legal SME in R1 prep; baseline posture conforms to JP 中小企業庁 修理権 + EU Right-to-Repair Directive 2024\n- N6 + N9 + N10 explicitly carve out OEM-cooperative pathways via Wave 2 ADRs; R0–R1 stays in OEM-cooperation-not-required envelope\n- L2 Li-ion bench borrowed from hikari R2 storage-battery cell (shared metrology); R1 single-vehicle trial validates standard\n- ASR mitigation via R3 thermal-recovery handoff to kanayama Wave 2 EAF (planned R3 milestone)\n\n## Alternatives Considered\n\n1. **Sub-cell of kanayama rather than dedicated Tier-B actor** — rejected: kanayama scope is post-shred metallurgy; ELV upstream chain (depollution + parts harvest + data wipe + right-to-repair catalog) is operationally distinct and demands its own constitutional gates (especially G8 data wipe + G12 right-to-repair, which are not metallurgy concerns).\n2. **Sub-cell of wadachi rather than dedicated Tier-B** — rejected: wadachi scope is autonomous-mobility R&D (vehicle build-side); ELV (vehicle end-side) is a different operational lifecycle stage with different SME requirements and different constitutional gates.\n3. **Bundle marine + aerospace + rail + automotive disassembly into one actor** — rejected: scope too large; each transport class has incompatible safety + chemistry + regulatory frameworks. R0 ground-vehicle-only with N2-N4 explicit non-goals.\n4. **Allow proprietary anti-disassembly DRM circumvention (rejected N6)** — rejected: §2(b) + legal-clarity invariant. OEM cooperation pathway preserved via Wave 2.\n5. **Allow chop-shop part re-VIN'ing (rejected N7 + N8)** — rejected: title invariant + §2(a) anti-organized-crime.\n6. **Drop G8 data wipe to \"best-effort\"** — rejected: §2(c) constitutional anti-surveillance is non-negotiable for adherent trust; if wipe fails, physical chip-shred is the fallback (slightly degraded material recovery is acceptable cost).\n7. **Drop G12 right-to-repair parts catalog** — rejected: §2(e) anti-gatekeeping is the constitutional reason this actor exists; parts catalog is the operational realization.\n8. **Allow military vehicle dismantling for ferrous recovery (rejected N1)** — rejected: §2(a) constitutional. Material value does not override Charter Rider.\n9. **R0 includes BEV cell-level recovery** — rejected: Tesla / VW MEB / GM Ultium proprietary cell architectures require OEM cooperation; deferred to Wave 2 ADR (N9).\n10. **R0 includes hydrogen fuel-cell vehicles** — rejected: H2 high-pressure tank disassembly safety class is fundamentally different; deferred to Wave 2 ADR (N10).\n\n## References\n\n- Source video methodology: YouTube `whyjio70IUU` \"How Audi Strips Down Thousand of Like-New Expensive Cars Inside Massive Facility\" (2026; manufacturing methodology adopted — depollution → parts harvest → shred → sort; OEM-monopoly right-to-repair-restricting layer rejected per §2(e))\n- ADR-2605192100 — etzhayyim mission charter (§1.13 Wellbecoming applied to vehicle ownership, §2(e) anti-gatekeeping)\n- ADR-2605192200 — Charter Rider v2.0 (§2(a-h) prohibited categories; §2(c) anti-surveillance basis for G8)\n- ADR-2605192415 — religious-corp daemon architecture (Tier-B definition)\n- ADR-2605242000 — wadachi autonomous mobility R0 (sibling — vehicle build side)\n- ADR-2605252400 — kanayama circular metallurgy R0 (sibling + downstream consumer; G2 mass-balance pattern inherited)\n- ADR-2605261115 — makura foam pillow R0 (sibling + downstream consumer for seat foam circular feed)\n- ADR-2605250715 — tatekata construction R0 (R2 yard-sharing partner)\n- ADR-2605201400 — kuni-umi planetary infra fleet (robotics class inheritance + Quad logistics)\n- ADR-2605214000 — Murakumo no-VKE mesh + lexicon port rules\n- ADR-2605215000 — etzhayyim inference Murakumo-fleet-only\n- ADR-2605191524 — Transparent Force swarm broadcast witness quorum\n- ADR-2605241500 — etzhayyim dataset CID substrate (IPFS-pinned parts catalog + emissions records)\n- ADR-2605181100 — XChaCha20-Poly1305 envelope (consent record + data wipe attestation encryption)\n- /CHARTER-RIDER.md — license addendum canonical text\n- 20-actors/hodoki/README.edn — actor scaffold\n- 20-actors/hodoki/manifest.jsonld — actor manifest (DID + cell registry + gates + non-goals)\n", :adr/path "90-docs/adr/2605261215-hodoki-elv-disassembly-tier-b-actor-r0.edn", :adr/source-repo "root", :adr/topic "hodoki-elv-disassembly-r0", :adr/last_verified "2026-05-25", :adr/date "2026-05-25", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/related ["wellbecoming-karma-lean-proofs" "wellbecoming-karma-lean-proofs" "wellbecoming-karma-lean-proofs" "wellbecoming-karma-lean-proofs"], :adr/authoritative_for ["hodoki actor identity (name, DID, tier, namespace, scope boundary) — R0 reservation" "ELV disassembly + materials recovery constitutional gates (G1..G14) and non-goals (N1..N10)" "R0 → R3 phased roadmap with R1/R2/R3 ADR reservation" "5-layer ELV processing chain (intake+depollute → battery → parts-harvest+catalyst+seat-textile → shred → emissions+provenance)" "9 Pregel cell catalog + Murakumo placement (R0 design-only)" "3 new robotics class reservation (Hagasu 剥がす / Nuku 抜く / Tokike 解け) + 4 kuni-umi inherited reuse" "lexicon namespace reservation (`com.etzhayyim.hodoki.*`, 8 record types)" "constitutional firsts: G8 mandatory ECU/infotainment data wipe (§2(c) anti-surveillance applied to vehicles) + G12 right-to-repair parts catalog invariant"]}]
